{
  "_what": "PRIXEL Mono glyph outlines, one per cell, for placing type on the plate.",
  "_coords": "Paths are already in the same space as assets/shapes/*.svg: 14.1732 units per 5mm cell, y down, origin at the cell's top-left. Drop them in exactly like a shape piece.",
  "_accents": "Diacritics are separate pieces that occupy the cell ABOVE the letter. There is NO acute; U+2019 (quote) is the stand-in - same mark, acute slope, but it sits 4.1mm above the letter against 2.0mm for a true grave.",
  "_substitutions": "case_group names the PHYSICAL piece. Several serve two characters when rotated (C/U, H/I, M/W, N/Z, 6/9, quotes, colon/diaeresis), so inventory must be counted per GROUP, not per character.",
